.TH QUADRF-APP 8 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-app \- start and stop exclusive QuadRF demo applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-app
.B status
.br
.B quadrf-app
.B start
.I app
.br
.B quadrf-app
.B stop
.I app
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts or stops a demo from the catalog in
.IR /usr/share/quadrf/apps.json .
The CSI and DSI front-end is single-client, so
.B start
stops every other exclusive app in that catalog, waits for the kernel to
release the device nodes, then starts the requested unit.
.PP
.B status
prints JSON with the installed and running state of each app. The web control
panel calls this helper through the sudoers rule in
.IR /etc/sudoers.d/quadrf .
.PP
Known
.I app
ids are
.BR ar
(Spatial RF Vision, headless WebSocket feed for
.IR /AR/ ),
.BR ntsc
(Camera Decoder) and
.BR psd
(PSD Plot). Desktop-launched copies of the same binaries are also killed, so a
session started from the VNC desktop does not keep the radio locked.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf (1),
.BR quadrf-rf-vision (1),
.BR quadrf-ntsc (1),
.BR quadrf-psd (1)
